{
  "_comment": "ORNL Flexible Research Platform (two-storey, one RTU + 10 VAV boxes with electric reheat) point -> CAMBER Role mapping, and the equipment each column belongs to (the ingest splits each one-day sheet into the RTU and its ten boxes: run group 'mapping'). Box ids nest under the RTU (RTU_VAV_<room>) so the naming topology puts each scenario's boxes under that scenario's RTU. One thermostat schedule serves every room (Table 3: 21/24 C occupied 7 a.m.-10 p.m., 15.6/29.4 C unoccupied), published once as the 'Terminal:' setpoint columns; the catalog's derive 'copy' gives each box its own CLGSP_/HTGSP_ copy, and the occupancy flag (OCC_<room>) likewise. RTU_FAN_ON is CAMBER's fan status, derived from supply-fan electricity above 5 Wh/min (300 W): the fan draws ~0.32 Wh/min (19 W) off and ~17-29 Wh/min on. Not mapped: the reheat coils (electric, logged as Wh per minute, not a valve or command, so reheat rules decline), compressor, condenser-fan and lighting energy, plug loads, room humidity (no zone-humidity role), the return damper (the complement of the OA damper in every row). Units: degC, m3/min (airflow), Pa (static), percent (dampers, humidity) -- declared on the catalog entry. Dataset: Im, Jung & Yoon 2025, Sci Data (doi:10.1038/s41597-025-05063-z), CC-BY-4.0.",
